  "authority": "Library of Congress / American Library Association, Urdu Romanization Table (2013 version; earlier 2011, 1997)",
  "description": "Library romanization of Urdu: retroflex ṭ ḍ ṛ, c for چ (ch is the aspirate چھ), aspirates written with h (bh, ph, ṭh …), k͟h and g͟h for خ and غ, ṉ for nūn ghunnah, majhūl vowels e and o, diphthongs ai and au, ʻ for ʿayn and ʼ for hamza; the Arabic article in names is joined to the preceding word (ʻAbdulʻazīz, Faẓlullāh).",
  "sources": [
    "https://www.loc.gov/catdir/cpso/romanization/urdu.pdf",
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romanization_of_Urdu"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Rule 18: the article is al- before moon letters, assimilated before sun letters (as-sijill), and inside a name its vowel is replaced by the final vowel of the preceding word and the parts are joined (ʻAbdulʻazīz, ʻAbdurrashīd, Abūlfaẓl, Zūlqarnain, Faẓlullāh). Implemented with post-processing; a consonant-final first element takes u.",
    "Rule 8: final ہ/ه is kept (guldastah, kih); unvocalised final h after a consonant is read -ah; after an aspirate it is dropped (mukh). Rule 14: shadda on و/ی gives vv/yy (quvvat, sayyid, Zakariyyā); a word-final -iyy is written ī here (not stated in the table).",
    "Rule 10 (ة and ت both t) is applied to unvocalised ة and to ۃ. Vocalised Arabic forms ending in fatḥah + ة (as supplied by the name lexicon for names Urdu writes with ہ, e.g. فاطمہ) are written -ah.",
    "Majhūl vowels: an unvocalised medial ی after a consonant is read e (sher), و is read o (dost); ī and ū need kasrah/ḍammah (or the lexicon). A final ی is ī, final ے is e.",
    "Rule 17 iẓāfat: -i after a consonant, -yi after a vowel, ۂ = -ah-yi (malikah-yi Inglistān). Rule 19 (conjunction و = o/va) is not automated.",
    "Diacritics lost in PDF extraction (ث s̱, ذ ẕ, ں ṉ, خ k͟h, غ g͟h) follow the research notes."
  ],
